# FS-UAE Launcher

This is the README file for FS-UAE Launcher.

## Installing FS-UAE Launcher

If you are using the source distribution, you should be able to install
FS-UAE Launcher by running "make install". The setup procedure
requires Python 3 and setuptools to be installed.

## Requirements

FS-UAE Launcher uses Qt 6 through `PySide6`, the `QtPy` compatibility
layer, and `QtAwesome` for scalable dashboard icons. Install the latest
releases supported by your Python version:

  python -m pip install --upgrade PySide6 QtPy QtAwesome requests

The Pipfile also declares these UI dependencies for Pipenv installations.
An existing virtual environment can be updated in place; recreating it is
not necessary:

  venv/bin/python -m pip install --upgrade PySide6 QtPy QtAwesome requests

The UI selects PySide6 by default. Use a clean process without another Qt
binding already imported; PyQt5 and PySide6 must not be mixed. Qt 6 handles
high-DPI scaling automatically. Existing explicitly selected themes are
preserved. Emulator, database, and networking behavior is unchanged.

It can optionally use the `lhafile` python package to support .lha archives.
The older packaging and INSTALL instructions still target Qt 5 and have not
been migrated as part of this UI-only change. Run from source with the
Python environment containing the Qt 6 dependencies.

## Modern Dark Workspace

Modern Dark is the default when no launcher theme has been selected. The
launcher opens maximized on its current display, with a 1080p-oriented
workspace, a labeled navigation rail, a searchable configuration library,
a resizable configuration editor, and persistent launch controls. All eight
configuration pages remain available. Settings, net play, tools, account
actions, and configuration warnings retain their existing behavior.

The library can be hidden with its toolbar toggle. Quick settings open in a
separate resizable pane, temporarily replacing the library below 1400 pixels
of window width. Screenshots and cover information use the selected
game's existing artwork; the media strip hides below 820 pixels of window
height so editing remains usable. The supported minimum window size is
1000 x 720. Long editor pages scroll rather than forcing a larger window.

Select Modern Dark in the Launcher settings and restart to replace a
previously saved theme. It can also be requested explicitly at startup:

  venv/bin/python fs-uae-launcher --launcher-theme=fusion-modern

Other saved themes retain the legacy window layout. QtAwesome is installed
in the project venv; other source installations must install it as above.

## UI Regression Tests

Run the widget, dialog, menu, painting, and screen tests without a display:

    QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen python -m unittest discover -s fsui/test -t .

Native file dialogs, multi-monitor placement, and platform-specific appearance
also need interactive testing on Linux, Windows, and macOS.
Image-button regression tests cover icon loading and activation, including
the launcher's New button, under PySide6.
Dashboard tests cover page routing, library/quick-settings toggles, the dark
palette, the theme picker, and 1920x1080, 1280x800, and 1000x720 layouts.
List-selection tests also verify that clearing a search selection emits None
rather than converting it to an incorrect row index under PySide6.

## GNOME Startup Compatibility

Some Qt/GNOME combinations abort during startup with a GLib error about the
missing `org.gnome.settings-daemon.plugins.xsettings` `antialiasing` key.
This is a desktop theme integration failure, not a missing Python package.
On Linux GNOME desktops the UI defaults to Qt's generic platform theme to
avoid that integration. Explicit `QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME` settings are respected;
other desktops and operating systems are unchanged. GNOME-specific theme and
file-dialog integration may differ with the generic platform theme.

To explicitly select the workaround when launching from a terminal:

  QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=generic venv/bin/python fs-uae-launcher

## Running FS-UAE Launcher

You start FS-UAE Launcher by running the following command:

    $ fs-uae-launcher

You can also run FS-UAE Launcher without installation by running the
following command in the source root directory:

    $ ./fs-uae-launcher

For an existing virtual environment, explicitly use its Python interpreter:

    $ venv/bin/python fs-uae-launcher

